Based originally on sun3_beaksoft.ps but improved quite a lot

You print this out on a transparency on your printer, flip it over so ink side is down and mount it on a piece of aluminum foil

At the top of the PostScript file you can change page size and strapline text, as well as grid spacing.

The tagline gets rendered backwards so that when you flip the transparency you print on it is legible.

render with GhostScript:
./bin/gs -dBATCH -dNOPAUSE -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -r1200 -sOutputFile=mousepad.pdf sun3_beaksoft.ps 

print it with:
lp -d EPSON_WF_3620_Series -o cupsPrintQuality=High mousepad.pdf

Remember to let the ink dry or it will smudge!

Enjoy

![screenshot](sun4_optical_mouse_pad.png)
